    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it's green. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` derivation following the existing `membershipTier` derived-field pattern in this codebase:\n\n1. **`Owner` model** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a fixed `CITY_REGION` table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`) and a derived getter `getLocality()` that returns the canonical region for the owner's city, or `\"UNKNOWN\"` when the city isn't in the table.\n\n2. **OpenAPI schema** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`) \u2014 declared `locality` as a read-only string property on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and MapStruct maps it from the model getter (exactly how `membershipTier` works).\n\nNo OfficeFloor endpoint changes were needed \u2014 `GET /api/owners/{ownerId}` already responds through `RespondWithOwner` \u2192 `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, which now includes the derived `locality`.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest` (the only test class) passes \u2014 both `coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` (Sydney \u2192 `NSW`) and `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` (random city \u2192 `UNKNOWN`) are green, and the full `./mvnw test` reports **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
